    <!--
      The versions of every artifact this reactor publishes that an application may declare: the runtime, the
      extensions, their -codegen bundles and -dev modules, the Dev Services and the test support (Vidocq/vidocq#339).
      vidocq-runtime-parent imports it; an application that keeps a parent of its own imports it alone:

          <dependencyManagement><dependencies><dependency>
              <groupId>io.vidocq.runtime</groupId><artifactId>vidocq-runtime-bom</artifactId>
              <version>…</version><type>pom</type><scope>import</scope>
          </dependency></dependencies></dependencyManagement>

      vidocq-parent is here for the release only: flatten-maven-plugin publishes a pom without a parent and without
      profiles, so an import brings these entries and nothing else. The versions are literal, as in the reactor
      root, so that versions:set keeps them current. ApplicationBomAndParentTest fails when a published module is
      missing.
    -->
